    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2-a8">

                <pb facs="0054" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg34"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dayton, United States minister, to Mr. Seward,
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1863-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 31,
                        1863</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><seg type="margin">[295]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * In my last conversation with Mr.
                    Drouyn de [295] Lhuys, he informed me that *Mr. Arman, the builder of these
                    vessels, was seeking purchasers for them other than the confederates, <pb
                        facs="0055" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/> and that the minister of marine did not
                    think himself authorized, therefore, to prevent their completion, although he
                    would prevent their being armed or delivered by Arman to the confederates.</p>
                <p>* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">WM. L. DAYTON.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
